    "readyState": "complete",
    "bodyText": "KEDDEH BRAINK Launchpad\n\nHTML authority surface · resident runtime projection · BTC Core node/server envelope\n\nHTML SURFACE: READY\nRUNTIME: UNBOUND\nBTC CORE: UNOBSERVED\nOverview\nBTC Protocol\nResident Linux\nBitcoin Core Node\nRuntime & Adapters\nSkill Fabric\nEvidence & Failures\nStorage & GitHub\nAuthority & Safety\nSystem Overview\nLAUNCH AUTHORITY\nHTML\n\nThe launchpad owns interaction, state visibility, routing intent and evidence projection.\n\nRESIDENT EXECUTION\nADAPTER-BOUND\n\nPython/host processes are execution manifestations, not UI authority.\n\nREPOSITORY ROLE\nSTORAGE\n\nGitHub stores/version-controls artifacts; it does not define product state.\n\nPRIMARY CAUSAL ROUTE\nHTML LAUNCHPAD\nRESIDENT BRIDGE\nBITCOIN CORE\nGETBLOCKTEMPLATE\nCANDIDATE\nSHA256D\nRECONSTRUCT\nSUBMITBLOCK\nCHAIN\nMATURITY\nSTATE OWNERSHIP\nUI / navigation\nHTML launchpad\nBTC protocol truth\nBitcoin Core + consensus rules\nExecution\nResident HTML Linux / V86 first; host adapters only where required\nEvidence\nReceipt ledger + immutable exported artifacts\nStorage\nLocal Library / Drive / GitHub version storage\nCURRENT BOUNDARY\n\nThis HTML file is a self-contained control surface. It does not claim to run bitcoind inside the browser. When bound to the resident bridge it becomes the operator console for the node server, mining runtime, evidence ledger and skill-governed workflows.\n\nKEX seed: KEX-HTML-LAUNCHPAD-20260819-7F2C91 · self-contained HTML launch surface · no external libraries",
